\subsection*{The original normalization and remaining closing condition}
For every fixed central-window parameter $M$, the governing
positive-source condition remains
\begin{equation}\label{eq:sc-original-obligation}
 \lim_{B\to\infty}\limsup_{m\to\infty}\sup_{R,n,k}
 m^2\operatorname*{ess\,sup}_{t\in\mathcal C_{m,R,n,k}(M)}
 \bigl(\mathsf U^{\rm low}_{B,m}(t)
                    -K_BP^{\rm ng}_{r_B,m}(t)\bigr)_+=0.
\end{equation}
The source, the original nongrazing comparison pool and their
same-roof meaning are those of the retained native reduction.
The whole positive physical sum precedes every supremum.
For each fixed $B$, all outer widths, comparison constants and
microscopic windows are fixed before the collision limsup.
The limit in $B$ is outermost. A proportional depth is used only
inside the displayed boundary estimates; it is not substituted into
the original microscopic guard.

The new regular boundary estimate resolves a specific previously
unpaid charge. The original same-roof positive-source comparison
still needs control of nonleading critical remainders and distinct
visited-grazing and other singular traces,
shallow low-incidence-load source, and sufficient true comparison
capacity, together with the remaining spectral, arithmetic and
conditional interfaces. A bound for collision volume, angular
measure, or roof total variation is not a bound for the roof
essential supremum in \eqref{eq:sc-original-obligation}.
No averaged limit theorem or alternative conditional event replaces
this target. The raw theorem and full inverse consequence are not
asserted complete.

