through native module 276; it does not review the later continuation.
It is an author-requested AI-assisted referee-style assessment,
not a journal decision or an independent specialist reconstruction.
The response locates all six major requests, four suggested closing
routes and nine secondary comments. Favorable A2 geometry reports
are excluded from A2-DYN review evidence.

The new geometric deductions use the complete native curve-class
verification in 281--283. Its use of the homogeneous growth lemma
of Demers--Zhang~\cite[Lemma 3.2(b), PDF p.~12]{DZUniform} is separated from their full
anisotropic spectral perturbation theorem, whose hypotheses are
stronger. Baladi--Demers~\cite{BDPressure} prove pressure results
with specific partition, potential and growth assumptions; these
are not supplied merely by cross-curve distortion. The tested
flow local limits of Dolgopyat--N\'andori~\cite{DNFlow} retain
their minimality, subgroup and observable hypotheses and do not
themselves yield our four-coordinate raw roof height.
General convex duality~\cite{BVNotes} provides background only;
the disk-word duality used here has its own retained full proof.
The literature audit records actual primary versions and theorem
locators, assumptions, function spaces and application limits.
Mathematical programs and compilation receipts provide auxiliary
reconstruction checks, not certification of continuum theorems
or journal suitability.

